Keep tool payloads and transcript text identical to the model-visible context.

Base: OpenClaw v2026.8.1 (ea806575e6450e4d1efdfc72c19f04be982a1b9b).
Backport of upstream #169063 (f956a18741): stop masking secret-shaped text when
tool arguments, tool results and conversation text are persisted to transcripts
or emitted as live tool events. The persisted copy diverged from the context the
model saw (for example 40-character relative paths matched the bare AWS secret
pattern), so the next run replayed different bytes and lost the provider prefix
cache from the first masked string onward.
Keep logging, diagnostic, telemetry and config redaction, image payload
stripping, and persisted detail size caps.
Remove when upgrading to an OpenClaw release that contains #169063.

